--- !u!114 &1099961539
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1099961537}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 32a1abd8e617d414a9d5784c5cb3e6a6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::KioskScreen
  font: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c43a2009fbd354dac999710313fe0abc, type: 2}
  accent: {r: 0.78431374, g: 0.627451, b: 0.41568628, a: 1}
  mapSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1634ca45fb36b4c709a0112b36eaea91, type: 3}
  wingId: W1
  sectionTitle: Ancient India
  period: "c. 1.5 million years ago \u2013 321 BCE"
  questions:
  - text: Which UNESCO World Heritage Site in Madhya Pradesh is famous for its prehistoric rock paintings?
    options:
    - Bhimbetka
    - Burzahom
    - Inamgaon
    - Bagor
    answer: 0
    why: Bhimbetka's rock shelters hold thousands of paintings, the earliest probably Mesolithic.
  - text: Which Harappan site, in the Rann of Kutch, had rock-cut reservoirs and a large signboard of Indus signs?
    options:
    - Lothal
    - Kalibangan
    - Rakhigarhi
    - Dholavira
    answer: 3
    why: Dholavira on Khadir island had remarkable reservoirs and a ten-sign signboard near a gateway.
  - text: How many hymns does the Rigveda contain?
    options:
    - 108
    - 400
    - 1,028
    - 10,000
    answer: 2
    why: The Rigveda has 1,028 hymns arranged in ten mandalas.
  - text: Where did the Buddha give his first sermon?
    options:
    - Bodh Gaya
    - Kushinagar
    - Sarnath
    - Lumbini
    answer: 2
    why: He attained enlightenment at Bodh Gaya and gave his first sermon at Sarnath.
  - text: How many great states, or mahajanapadas, do Buddhist and Jain texts list?
    options:
    - Seven
    - Twelve
    - Sixteen
    - Twenty-four
    answer: 2
    why: The texts list sixteen mahajanapadas around the 6th century BCE.
  - text: Which Persian king conquered Gandhara and the Indus region in the late 6th century BCE?
    options:
    - Cyrus the Great
    - Xerxes
    - Darius the First
    - Artaxerxes
    answer: 2
    why: Darius I made the region a tribute-paying province of the Achaemenid empire.
  entries:
  - year: -10000
    label: Mesolithic period onwards (from c. 10,000 BCE)
    title: Rock paintings of Bhimbetka
    credit: 'Photo: Yann (talk) / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons'
    target: {fileID: 1134456657}
    photo: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 29d7720454ef44e67a906f32e402b885, type: 3}
    places:
    - name: Bhimbetka
      u: 0.3781
      v: 0.5051
  - year: -2000
    label: "c. 2000\u20131900 BCE"
    title: The 'Priest-King'
    credit: 'Photo: Mamoon Mengal / CC BY-SA 1.0 / Wikimedia Commons'
    target: {fileID: 674983424}
    photo: {fileID: 21300000, guid: df6868062f1f44a92be6a451a3c7fd83, type: 3}
    places:
    - name: Mohenjo-daro
      u: 0.115
      v: 0.6371
  - year: -2100
    label: "c. 2300\u20131750 BCE"
    title: The 'Dancing Girl'
    credit: 'Photo: Gary Todd / CC0 / Wikimedia Commons'
    target: {fileID: 1029109011}
    photo: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 32f2cb3e25dc04b738ffc92f32e2d26f, type: 3}
    places:
